  "fault_interpretation": "0x10 is latched when input HV detection (CHR_CON0 bit 7) or battery OV detection (CHR_CON6 bit 6) asserts. Both are clear in the later inhibited snapshot. The first-fault detector registers were not retained, so the exact detector and electrical cause cannot be established from this capture.",
  "source_comparison": "The actual stock charging_hw_init passes selector 1 to upmu_set_rg_vbat_ov_vth (4.3 V in retained BSP). Linux still has selector 0 at register 0x000c=0x0001 and deliberately preserves it. Its precise threshold is unresolved. This is a diagnostic lead, not permission to raise the protection threshold or proof of the fault cause.",
  "earlier_wall_session": "Not observable in this boot: offline=0, no Y2CHARGE history, /data/logs empty, /var/log points to volatile /tmp, and no /sys/fs/pstore interface. The owner report remains separate from this PC-connected fault.",
